+## Phase 3 Slice 3 Certified Evidence
+
+- Logical case identity is now `organizationId + checkKey + definitionVersion + sourceType + sourceId`, enforced directly by a Prisma unique key.
+- Fingerprints are versioned and stable across source hash, status, severity, evidence, evidence grade, and recommended-action changes.
+- Registry-owned definition version is rebound on permission, missing-runner, successful runner, and runner-error paths; spoofed result identity is rejected before persistence.
+- Active evidence drift updates one row with `SOURCE_CHANGED` and audit history without a new alert.
+- Changed evidence reopens the same `RESOLVED`, `WAIVED`, or `CLOSED` row with one reopen alert; `SUPPRESSED` remains suppressed without an alert.
+- Serializable upsert retries only expected Prisma unique or serialization races and fails safely after two attempts.
+- The migration fails closed on pre-existing logical duplicates and performs no merge, delete, update, or backfill.
+- Disposable PostgreSQL certification passes 5/5 concurrency and lifecycle scenarios with the normal application client; direct migration certification proves clean install and duplicate rollback.
+- Focused final verification passes 5 suites/69 tests; expanded assurance verification passes 7 suites/73 tests with 5 environment-gated PostgreSQL tests skipped.
+- Full repository TypeScript, focused ESLint, Prisma validation, Workflow Assurance release/runtime gates, service boundary, module surface, role cockpit, and migration-safety gates pass.
+- The policy chain remains held only by the unrelated statutory source-artifact hash and expert-approval requirements.
+- No detector, POS source, dashboard, action, inventory behavior, generic resolution-policy change, AI, or WhatsApp work was added.
+
+Evidence: `what-next/referrals/WORKFLOW_ASSURANCE_STABLE_CASE_IDENTITY_REPORT_2026-07-20.md`.
+
